WEBVTT

00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:08.635
Oh, I wonder what that's about.

00:00:08.757 --> 00:00:10.561
I'm not here.

00:00:11.331 --> 00:00:12.608
Wait...

00:00:12.932 --> 00:00:15.324
The police are looking for you?

00:00:18.648 --> 00:00:20.087
What police?

00:00:22.025 --> 00:00:24.566
Hey, guys, guess what.
It's our birthday in two weeks.

00:00:24.601 --> 00:00:25.667
You're kidding.

00:00:25.702 --> 00:00:29.720
- You all have birthdays on the same day?
- No, no, no, but we decided that,

00:00:29.755 --> 00:00:32.240
seeing that birthdays are
so generally unpleasant...

00:00:32.274 --> 00:00:33.708
Depressing, scary...

00:00:33.742 --> 00:00:36.080
Drunken, hazy...

00:00:36.114 --> 00:00:40.138
We decided that we'd just celebrate
ours all together on a neutral day.

00:00:40.173 --> 00:00:42.576
And that way we don't
have to acknowledge

00:00:42.610 --> 00:00:44.763
the day that we
actually get older.

00:00:44.797 --> 00:00:48.933
It works great. I really
don't know how old I am.

00:00:48.967 --> 00:00:50.617
So what do you guys
want for your birthday?

00:00:50.651 --> 00:00:52.433
A wonderful man
who worships me.

00:00:52.467 --> 00:00:55.282
- Two of those.
- Oh, that sounds nice.

00:00:55.316 --> 00:00:58.102
Why don't you all get each
other dates for your birthday?

00:00:58.137 --> 00:01:00.420
Now, that is an
intriguing idea.

00:01:00.454 --> 00:01:02.869
I mean, we're terrible at
picking men for ourselves.

00:01:02.904 --> 00:01:05.225
I have five divorces
to prove it.

00:01:05.259 --> 00:01:06.857
I wish I had a divorce.

00:01:06.892 --> 00:01:08.592
I have animals that die.

00:01:10.766 --> 00:01:11.610
Let's do it.

00:01:11.642 --> 00:01:14.768
Everyone's gonna pick a name,
and then get a date for that person.

00:01:14.802 --> 00:01:17.539
It'll be our new Cleveland
birthday celebration.

00:01:17.574 --> 00:01:19.474
And where are we going
to find these men?

00:01:19.508 --> 00:01:21.580
They do seem to be
all over this town.

00:01:21.614 --> 00:01:25.784
I get disgusting comments and lewd
gestures, like, ten times a day.

00:01:25.804 --> 00:01:27.345
It is fantastic!

00:01:29.419 --> 00:01:31.334
Elka, are you in?

00:01:31.369 --> 00:01:32.384
Sure.

00:01:33.133 --> 00:01:35.060
But if you're picking for me,

00:01:35.095 --> 00:01:36.600
I don't do fatties.

00:01:41.387 --> 00:01:43.927
Okay, Elka, you go first.

00:01:46.981 --> 00:01:47.931
Victoria.

00:01:47.974 --> 00:01:50.015
- Melanie.
- Elka.

00:01:50.049 --> 00:01:51.890
Oh, great that means
Victoria got me.

00:01:51.925 --> 00:01:52.591
So?

00:01:52.626 --> 00:01:54.398
So you're terrible
at picking gifts.

00:01:54.432 --> 00:01:56.798
- I'm gonna get screwed.
- Oh, stop it!

00:01:56.833 --> 00:01:58.898
I'm a wonderful gift giver.

00:01:58.932 --> 00:02:02.732
See, look at this beautiful
pre-birthday gift I just gave myself.

00:02:02.888 --> 00:02:05.300
Wow, Cartier. My favorite.

00:02:05.382 --> 00:02:07.748
But you didn't even remember
it was <i>our</i> birthday.

00:02:07.783 --> 00:02:09.620
Still, it's a great gift.

00:02:22.862 --> 00:02:24.965
I wonder when our
presents will arrive.

00:02:24.999 --> 00:02:26.302
Yours will be here soon.

00:02:26.337 --> 00:02:28.307
I wish the same could
be said for mine.

00:02:28.341 --> 00:02:30.511
I'm sure Victoria
didn't find me anyone.

00:02:30.545 --> 00:02:33.580
Oh, don't be so negative.
I got Elka a great date.

00:02:33.615 --> 00:02:35.255
I'm a little nervous.

00:02:36.149 --> 00:02:40.299
Or maybe it's just staring at that
rat's nest that Joy calls a hairdo.

00:02:42.003 --> 00:02:44.174
It's so unsettling.

00:02:44.951 --> 00:02:48.047
Your nerves are making
you unpleasant.

00:02:48.082 --> 00:02:51.053
Yes, but I can fix that
by finishing this wine.

00:02:51.088 --> 00:02:53.726
You're still stuck
with that hair.

00:02:54.627 --> 00:02:57.633
That's not your joke, Elka.
That's Winston Churchill's.

00:02:57.668 --> 00:03:00.572
It's not stealing
if you were there.

00:03:04.061 --> 00:03:05.711
Elka, your date's here.

00:03:08.127 --> 00:03:09.890
He's handsome!

00:03:09.925 --> 00:03:12.130
- Where did you find him?
- At a senior center.

00:03:12.164 --> 00:03:14.668
I emailed your photo over to see
if anybody would be interested.

00:03:14.702 --> 00:03:17.540
He was the only one who
knew how to email back.

00:03:17.574 --> 00:03:19.097
Hey, Max.

00:03:19.845 --> 00:03:23.652
Melanie, so nice to
officially meet you.

00:03:23.687 --> 00:03:25.556
And you must be Elka.

00:03:25.590 --> 00:03:26.693
I am.

00:03:26.774 --> 00:03:30.656
May I say that you're even
lovelier than in your picture?

00:03:31.264 --> 00:03:33.041
Yes, you may.

00:03:33.365 --> 00:03:34.966
Shall we?

00:03:35.007 --> 00:03:36.472
To be fair,

00:03:36.507 --> 00:03:39.941
in my computer, your picture
is displayed in 200%.

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:41.928
I've seen all of you, but

00:03:41.963 --> 00:03:43.686
not all at once.

00:04:00.604 --> 00:04:03.381
- Uh, excuse me.
- Yeah.

00:04:03.415 --> 00:04:05.851
- I'm Victoria Chase.
- Hi.

00:04:05.885 --> 00:04:08.655
How would you like to pretend
to be my friend's date?

00:04:08.689 --> 00:04:10.759
Uh, what's the matter with her?

00:04:10.793 --> 00:04:12.628
Nothing, really.
She's quite attractive.

00:04:12.663 --> 00:04:15.467
She's sitting right over there
with the long brown hair.

00:04:15.501 --> 00:04:17.170
- Oh...
- I'll give you 200 bucks.

00:04:17.204 --> 00:04:19.340
- Great!
- Wait, wait, wait.

00:04:19.374 --> 00:04:21.142
But you can't be yourself.

00:04:21.177 --> 00:04:22.511
I mean, I'm sure you're great,

00:04:22.545 --> 00:04:25.648
but I was supposed to find
her a specific type of guy.

00:04:25.682 --> 00:04:27.550
Well, why didn't you if you
said you were going to?

00:04:27.584 --> 00:04:30.820
Well, I ran out of time,
or I didn't prioritize, or...

00:04:30.854 --> 00:04:33.354
I don't know,
I just-- get off my back!

00:04:34.891 --> 00:04:36.124
What do you do?

00:04:36.158 --> 00:04:38.292
Well, with the economy
and everything--

00:04:38.326 --> 00:04:40.694
okay, I'm bored already.

00:04:40.728 --> 00:04:43.329
You are an architect.
She goes crazy for them.

00:04:43.364 --> 00:04:45.114
Okay...

00:04:45.199 --> 00:04:47.166
And you have three dogs,
but not purebreds.

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:50.435
She'd never go for that.
Let's see, what else?

00:04:50.470 --> 00:04:53.071
Oh, compliment her earlobes.
Don't ask me why.

00:04:53.105 --> 00:04:54.939
Favorite color, celadon.

00:04:54.974 --> 00:04:57.575
Don't order beets,
and do not mention Helen Mirren.

00:04:57.609 --> 00:05:00.173
- What's your name?
- Uh, Steve.

00:05:00.213 --> 00:05:04.145
No, no, I think that
you are an Alistair.

00:05:04.179 --> 00:05:07.506
- Then I think I need another 50.
- Okay, Steve's good.

00:05:08.516 --> 00:05:10.083
Well, I'll be damned.

00:05:10.117 --> 00:05:11.851
These are my friends
Melanie and Joy.

00:05:11.885 --> 00:05:13.986
- Hi.
- And this is Steve.

00:05:14.020 --> 00:05:15.591
He's an architect.

00:05:16.791 --> 00:05:17.853
I am.

00:05:19.395 --> 00:05:20.695
And I like dogs.

00:05:22.059 --> 00:05:23.259
I love dogs.

00:05:24.593 --> 00:05:25.700
You have dogs?

00:05:25.734 --> 00:05:28.302
Yes, yes. Uh, mutts.

00:05:28.336 --> 00:05:30.203
I mean I love all dogs,

00:05:30.238 --> 00:05:33.339
but I just don't see the
point of buying a dog

00:05:33.373 --> 00:05:36.641
from an industry that promotes
inbreeding and puppyvilles

00:05:36.676 --> 00:05:39.606
when there are so many mixed breeds
out there in need of a home.

00:05:39.641 --> 00:05:41.945
I feel exactly the same way.

00:05:41.979 --> 00:05:43.913
Well, should I try to
go round us up a table?

00:05:43.947 --> 00:05:45.814
- Sounds great.
- All right.

00:05:45.848 --> 00:05:47.098
So...

00:05:47.516 --> 00:05:50.206
I owe you an apology.

00:05:50.246 --> 00:05:52.451
You truly are a
wonderful friend

00:05:52.485 --> 00:05:54.953
who seems to have
found me a great guy.

00:05:54.988 --> 00:05:57.258
I'm sorry. I really
underestimated you.

00:05:57.293 --> 00:06:00.662
Oh, well,
I accept your apology.

00:06:00.696 --> 00:06:02.696
You are free to enjoy him now.

00:06:04.835 --> 00:06:08.485
I can't believe you went to that
much work to find Joy's date.

00:06:08.642 --> 00:06:10.872
But you <i>do</i> believe it, right?

00:06:13.309 --> 00:06:15.910
Oh, Happy Birthday.

00:06:15.944 --> 00:06:17.611
Do you think he's
here for one of us?

00:06:17.646 --> 00:06:19.379
Oh, he's looking over here.
How do I look?

00:06:19.414 --> 00:06:20.905
Freakishly young.

00:06:20.940 --> 00:06:23.911
- What about me? How's my hair?
- Like God re-touched it.

00:06:23.946 --> 00:06:25.344
- Good luck.
- You too.

00:06:25.345 --> 00:06:28.345
- Uh, Victoria?
- Yes!

00:06:29.155 --> 00:06:31.557
Sorry I'm late. I had to jog
the last couple of blocks

00:06:31.591 --> 00:06:34.926
just to get here,
but it was worth it--wow.

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:37.796
Are all actresses as
beautiful in person as you?

00:06:37.831 --> 00:06:38.831
Sadly, no.

00:06:41.832 --> 00:06:44.466
Glenn Miller or Tommy Dorsey?

00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:46.702
Oh, Miller all the way.

00:06:46.736 --> 00:06:48.237
Yeah, that was real music.

00:06:48.271 --> 00:06:51.171
I don't go for that stuff
that's out there now.

00:06:51.239 --> 00:06:52.439
Michael Buble.

00:06:54.477 --> 00:06:56.577
Have you heard this yahoo?

00:06:57.211 --> 00:06:59.513
Please! You mean
wannabe Sinatra.

00:06:59.547 --> 00:07:00.914
Exactly.

00:07:00.948 --> 00:07:04.617
Go back to the second floor
at Nordstrom's, I say.

00:07:05.460 --> 00:07:07.485
Okay, another question:

00:07:07.923 --> 00:07:09.423
Favorite medication.

00:07:12.158 --> 00:07:13.908
Oh, that's a tough one.

00:07:15.271 --> 00:07:18.676
All things considered,
I think I'm gonna have to say

00:07:18.818 --> 00:07:19.818
Celebrex.

00:07:20.527 --> 00:07:22.360
Celebrex. Nice.

00:07:22.648 --> 00:07:25.863
I'm an allopurinol man myself.

00:07:25.898 --> 00:07:27.330
Ooh, gout!

00:07:28.169 --> 00:07:29.869
Somebody likes to party.

00:07:32.641 --> 00:07:35.291
Ever go to Canada for
your discount rates?

00:07:36.879 --> 00:07:41.148
Do I? I'm on a first-name basis
with all the border guards.

00:07:41.857 --> 00:07:43.201
Me too.

00:07:43.236 --> 00:07:45.136
We should carpool next time.

00:07:47.071 --> 00:07:50.155
Is it possible that you
are the perfect woman?

00:07:50.885 --> 00:07:53.824
Well, I'd say it's
very possible.

00:07:55.644 --> 00:07:57.861
Will you be eating alone?
I can bring over a place setting.

00:07:57.896 --> 00:08:00.129
Oh, no, no, no, no.
I--I have a date.

00:08:00.163 --> 00:08:01.629
It's a blind date.
He should be here soon.

00:08:01.663 --> 00:08:03.462
I'm sure he will.
Anything else?

00:08:03.496 --> 00:08:05.163
I'm really nervous.

00:08:05.198 --> 00:08:07.332
I haven't been on a blind date in,
like, oh, gosh, forever.

00:08:07.366 --> 00:08:08.633
I just got divorced.

00:08:08.667 --> 00:08:10.534
I'm totally over it.
It's just, you know,

00:08:10.568 --> 00:08:12.869
sometimes it still feels
a little fresh and raw.

00:08:12.904 --> 00:08:14.280
But this is just the
type of adventure

00:08:14.315 --> 00:08:16.621
I signed up for when I moved
to Cleveland, isn't it?

00:08:16.656 --> 00:08:20.141
Uh, I was just wondering if
you need a fork or something.

00:08:22.499 --> 00:08:23.399
Melanie?

00:08:23.639 --> 00:08:24.379
Yes?

00:08:26.884 --> 00:08:28.684
I think I'm gonna be sick.

00:08:32.154 --> 00:08:34.563
I'm so sorry.
That didn't come out right.

00:08:34.598 --> 00:08:36.998
It's just your face
is kind of--oh...

00:08:40.124 --> 00:08:42.181
Sorry, I'm feeling
queasy again.

00:08:42.216 --> 00:08:44.648
Why don't we just leave
it at I'm not your type?

00:08:44.668 --> 00:08:47.310
No, no, no, actually,
you're totally my type.

00:08:47.330 --> 00:08:49.630
You look exactly
like my dead wife.

00:08:51.189 --> 00:08:53.566
- Uh...Thank you?
- Yeah.

00:08:54.033 --> 00:08:55.593
Listen, this is obviously
upsetting for you,

00:08:55.627 --> 00:08:57.494
so let's just not do
the whole date thing.

00:08:57.529 --> 00:09:00.463
Oh, listen, I really need
to move on with my life,

00:09:00.497 --> 00:09:03.265
and this is the first actual
date I've had since the funeral.

00:09:03.299 --> 00:09:06.334
And Joy said so many nice things
about you in line at the deli.

00:09:06.368 --> 00:09:08.979
You know what, I don't know
if this is a real good idea.

00:09:08.999 --> 00:09:09.999
Please?

00:09:10.387 --> 00:09:14.506
If I have to spend another night alone,
I don't know what I'll do.

00:09:17.123 --> 00:09:18.409
Why not?

00:09:18.866 --> 00:09:20.911
Life's too short, right?

00:09:21.247 --> 00:09:22.497
I'm so sorry.

00:09:26.470 --> 00:09:27.457
So where were we?

00:09:27.492 --> 00:09:30.338
You were telling me how you all
picked dates for each other.

00:09:30.373 --> 00:09:32.552
- That's fun.
- Oh, it is fun.

00:09:33.013 --> 00:09:35.114
Especially when it looks
like I got the prize.

00:09:35.148 --> 00:09:37.082
Oh, I'm flattered.

00:09:37.116 --> 00:09:38.483
You'll have to excuse me,
I'm still sweating.

00:09:38.517 --> 00:09:41.051
That run over here was a bit
further than I anticipated.

00:09:41.085 --> 00:09:42.252
Oh. Do you mind?

00:09:42.286 --> 00:09:43.519
No, not at all.

00:09:43.554 --> 00:09:46.454
You just take off as much
clothing as you like.

00:09:57.316 --> 00:10:00.267
You know, I never formally
introduced myself.

00:10:00.301 --> 00:10:01.401
I'm Chester.

00:10:05.138 --> 00:10:06.539
Chester.

00:10:06.573 --> 00:10:08.823
Well, that'll be
easy to remember.

00:10:11.076 --> 00:10:13.226
The truth is I'm
a great driver,

00:10:13.755 --> 00:10:17.212
but sometimes I like
to drive real slow

00:10:17.246 --> 00:10:18.996
just to mess with people.

00:10:21.538 --> 00:10:24.417
I am having such a good time.

00:10:24.452 --> 00:10:26.052
Me too.

00:10:26.469 --> 00:10:29.122
I think we should get married.

00:10:29.156 --> 00:10:32.357
Me too. Pass the salt.

00:10:32.391 --> 00:10:35.060
Really? You'd marry me?

00:10:35.094 --> 00:10:36.896
Yeah, I would.

00:10:37.133 --> 00:10:41.067
I mean once around we're
perfect for each other.

00:10:41.101 --> 00:10:43.335
I'm glad to hear that.

00:10:43.370 --> 00:10:46.304
Oh, here's your salt.

00:10:46.339 --> 00:10:48.940
I'm impressed you
can still use that.

00:10:48.975 --> 00:10:51.977
Oh, I know how to
shake what I've got.

00:10:57.246 --> 00:11:00.115
I've been wanting to
do that all night.

00:11:00.150 --> 00:11:02.417
Oh...Well...

00:11:02.451 --> 00:11:06.821
Now I can get back
to my rigatoni.

00:11:06.887 --> 00:11:07.932
Celadon?

00:11:08.170 --> 00:11:10.271
Most men don't even
know what that is.

00:11:10.305 --> 00:11:13.205
Well...I do.

00:11:13.674 --> 00:11:16.475
So becoming an architect
was like a calling?

00:11:16.509 --> 00:11:19.944
Yes. Yes, it was like someone
tapped me on the shoulder

00:11:19.978 --> 00:11:22.128
and said,
"you're an architect."

00:11:24.314 --> 00:11:27.182
And I'll start with
the Caesar salad.

00:11:27.217 --> 00:11:29.785
Hey, have you ever thought
about wearing your hair,

00:11:29.819 --> 00:11:32.188
I don't know,
back a little bit?

00:11:33.448 --> 00:11:37.057
- Excuse me?
- Just push it back on the sides.

00:11:37.092 --> 00:11:39.659
That--that's too much.
A little less.

00:11:39.694 --> 00:11:42.262
Oh, God, it's uncanny!

00:11:42.296 --> 00:11:45.696
This is gonna sound crazy,
but you look so much like her.

00:11:46.046 --> 00:11:47.896
I gotta show you a picture.

00:11:49.330 --> 00:11:50.834
How's your pasta?

00:11:50.868 --> 00:11:52.568
Fine. How's your breast?

00:11:56.179 --> 00:11:57.440
It's a meatloaf.

00:11:57.474 --> 00:11:58.724
I'll say it is.

00:12:01.365 --> 00:12:02.279
Victoria.

00:12:02.314 --> 00:12:03.647
Excuse me, my friend--

00:12:03.681 --> 00:12:05.181
needs me at the bar.

00:12:08.386 --> 00:12:11.721
You're not gonna believe this, but my date
is trying to turn me into his dead wife.

00:12:11.756 --> 00:12:13.096
Okay, that's nothing.

00:12:13.131 --> 00:12:15.260
You seen the cans on Chester?

00:12:23.726 --> 00:12:27.567
And his name is "chester"?

00:12:27.602 --> 00:12:30.837
Would you ask our waitress to bring
us a bottle of champagne, please?

00:12:30.871 --> 00:12:34.139
Champagne!
You really came through.

00:12:34.173 --> 00:12:36.473
- You're a good friend.
- Aren't I?

00:12:36.508 --> 00:12:39.210
Oh, hey, hey, Victoria,
thanks again.

00:12:39.245 --> 00:12:41.395
Best blind date
I have ever had.

00:12:47.685 --> 00:12:51.253
I am not gonna let
this one get away.

00:12:54.557 --> 00:12:56.557
Oh, boy.

00:12:59.369 --> 00:13:01.941
You set Joy up with a murderer?

00:13:02.002 --> 00:13:05.690
Well, to be fair, at the time I just
thought he was a complete stranger.

00:13:05.725 --> 00:13:08.336
Now, can we just focus and figure
out what we should do next?

00:13:08.363 --> 00:13:10.330
There's a tip line
number on the screen.

00:13:10.364 --> 00:13:12.766
It's ringing. Oh, my God,
how did this happen?

00:13:12.800 --> 00:13:15.568
Well, I kinda sorta picked him
when I came in here tonight.

00:13:15.602 --> 00:13:19.338
I gave him 200 bucks and told
him to show her a good time.

00:13:19.372 --> 00:13:23.007
So he's a murderer
<i>and</i> a hooker!

00:13:23.042 --> 00:13:25.510
Oh, hello, hello!
Yes, this is Melanie Moretti.

00:13:25.544 --> 00:13:27.644
The suspect that
you're looking for

00:13:27.679 --> 00:13:29.413
is at Stormy's on Euclid.

00:13:29.447 --> 00:13:32.295
And the only thing I
hate more than beets

00:13:32.336 --> 00:13:33.636
is Helen Mirren.

00:13:35.451 --> 00:13:37.451
Kiss me.

00:13:38.120 --> 00:13:40.254
Hurry! Hurry!
He's kissing her!

00:13:41.012 --> 00:13:42.222
Okay, thank you.

00:13:42.257 --> 00:13:44.758
Okay, he said to stay
calm and act normal.

00:13:44.792 --> 00:13:47.202
And we have to try and keep
him here until they arrive.

00:13:47.215 --> 00:13:49.796
Okay, well, let's just get rid of
our dates so that we can focus.

00:13:49.830 --> 00:13:53.930
Oh, gosh, you know, considering
everything, maybe my date's not so bad.

00:13:56.669 --> 00:13:58.219
Oh, who am I kidding?

00:14:00.202 --> 00:14:02.540
- Everything okay?
- Wow...

00:14:02.575 --> 00:14:04.875
That jacket really
does wonders for you.

00:14:04.910 --> 00:14:06.610
Yeah, I got it
right off the rack.

00:14:06.644 --> 00:14:10.144
Don't say rack.

00:14:10.614 --> 00:14:12.048
Listen, Chester,

00:14:12.082 --> 00:14:14.150
I don't think it's gonna
work out between us.

00:14:14.184 --> 00:14:16.685
But we didn't even
finish dinner yet.

00:14:16.719 --> 00:14:17.986
Sorry for whatever
it is I did wrong.

00:14:18.020 --> 00:14:20.455
Wait, wait. Come here.

00:14:20.489 --> 00:14:25.625
Um, excuse me, do you
find this man attractive?

00:14:25.660 --> 00:14:26.793
And she's cute, right?

00:14:26.827 --> 00:14:28.128
- Yeah.
- Good. Great.

00:14:28.162 --> 00:14:29.595
Why don't you sit down
and buy her a drink.

00:14:29.630 --> 00:14:30.796
- Really?
- Really.

00:14:30.831 --> 00:14:32.631
- Well, okay.
- No, no, no.

00:14:32.665 --> 00:14:36.667
Keep that on...Forever.

00:14:36.701 --> 00:14:38.951
Let's go.

00:14:39.171 --> 00:14:40.371
I suppose you're right.

00:14:40.406 --> 00:14:42.473
I guess I wasn't really ready
to get out there after all.

00:14:42.507 --> 00:14:44.774
You know what, it's okay. It's okay.
It was very nice to meet you,

00:14:44.808 --> 00:14:45.775
and I wish you
nothing but the best.

00:14:45.809 --> 00:14:47.643
You know, I think why

00:14:47.677 --> 00:14:49.311
my wife's death
is so hard on me

00:14:49.345 --> 00:14:51.513
is that I never got a
chance to say good-bye.

00:14:51.547 --> 00:14:53.815
I got to the hospital
ten minutes too late.

00:14:53.850 --> 00:14:55.984
Oh, you poor thing.

00:14:56.018 --> 00:14:58.486
I know this is gonna sound odd,

00:14:58.520 --> 00:15:00.621
but with you being
so much like her,

00:15:00.655 --> 00:15:02.356
I feel like it would
help give me closure

00:15:02.390 --> 00:15:04.458
if I could say good-bye
to you in the way

00:15:04.492 --> 00:15:06.026
that I wanted to say
good-bye to her.

00:15:06.060 --> 00:15:09.328
Oh, you know,
that's-- I don't know.

00:15:09.363 --> 00:15:11.296
- Yeah, it's too much.
- Yeah.

00:15:11.331 --> 00:15:15.200
- I get it. I'll go.
- Okay. Okay.

00:15:15.234 --> 00:15:17.936
Oh, go ahead, say good-bye.

00:15:17.970 --> 00:15:20.471
Oh, thank you.

00:15:23.574 --> 00:15:26.842
Honey, you're the most
amazing woman I've ever met.

00:15:28.197 --> 00:15:31.597
Your strength, grace,
and courage will be with me always.

00:15:31.700 --> 00:15:32.750
I love you.

00:15:33.251 --> 00:15:34.301
Okey-dokey!

00:15:37.321 --> 00:15:39.887
May I give her a little kiss?

00:15:39.922 --> 00:15:43.290
It's me, not her.
But whatever.

00:15:46.445 --> 00:15:50.403
I'd give anything to make
love to her one last time.

00:15:51.700 --> 00:15:53.730
And we're done here.

00:15:55.833 --> 00:15:57.567
Guess what happened to me!

00:15:57.602 --> 00:15:59.485
Elka, not now. We're in
the middle of a crisis.

00:15:59.506 --> 00:16:00.870
I got engaged.

00:16:05.241 --> 00:16:07.375
- I knew you'd like him!
- He's amazing.

00:16:07.410 --> 00:16:10.110
Oh, no, he's paying the bill!
He's gonna go. We have to keep him here.

00:16:10.145 --> 00:16:11.111
Oh, my God,
what are we gonna do?

00:16:11.145 --> 00:16:15.048
Who cares about Joy? What about me?
I'm getting married.

00:16:15.082 --> 00:16:18.083
I'm, like, 100!

00:16:18.118 --> 00:16:23.554
Listen, Victoria accidentally
set Joy up with a murderer.

00:16:25.590 --> 00:16:28.592
I'm conflicted.

00:16:31.593 --> 00:16:33.563
I am on a great date
for once in my life,

00:16:33.598 --> 00:16:34.898
and you guys are
acting like idiots.

00:16:34.932 --> 00:16:36.232
What's going on?

00:16:36.873 --> 00:16:40.402
Uh, well, I waited
until the last minute,

00:16:40.437 --> 00:16:43.205
and I just grabbed the first
guy I could find a the bar,

00:16:43.239 --> 00:16:45.607
and I gave him $200
to be your date.

00:16:45.641 --> 00:16:49.243
What? You paid Steve
to go out with me?

00:16:49.278 --> 00:16:51.678
This is all fake?

00:16:51.713 --> 00:16:54.488
Oh, my God, this is, like,
the worst thing you've ever done to me.

00:16:54.523 --> 00:16:56.104
Well, there's more.

00:16:58.617 --> 00:17:02.388
- Uh, he's kind of a...Murderer.
- What?

00:17:02.423 --> 00:17:05.291
But the police
are on their way.

00:17:05.326 --> 00:17:06.560
Guys, he's coming.

00:17:06.594 --> 00:17:08.228
Okay, listen, we have to
try and keep him here,

00:17:08.262 --> 00:17:09.296
so just act natural.

00:17:09.330 --> 00:17:11.431
How do I act natural
with a murderer?

00:17:11.465 --> 00:17:13.599
Just do the opposite of that.

00:17:14.984 --> 00:17:16.902
So, Joy, are you ready to go?

00:17:16.936 --> 00:17:20.304
My van's parked out front.

00:17:20.969 --> 00:17:22.104
Your van?

00:17:22.144 --> 00:17:24.673
He has a <i>van!</i>

00:17:24.707 --> 00:17:25.740
Are you okay?

00:17:25.774 --> 00:17:27.742
- Why don't you join us for dessert?
- Yes.

00:17:27.776 --> 00:17:30.044
You know, to be honest,
I was just...

00:17:30.078 --> 00:17:31.211
Hoping to get Joy alone.

00:17:31.246 --> 00:17:33.714
No! I mean-- tell
me what I mean!

00:17:33.748 --> 00:17:36.449
- She has a rare disease.
- Joy's a lesbian.

00:17:36.484 --> 00:17:37.484
Hey.

00:17:38.485 --> 00:17:39.485
Oh, God!

00:17:43.956 --> 00:17:46.367
Now can we talk
about my engagement?

00:17:54.626 --> 00:17:56.827
As soon as he was on the
floor writhing in pain,

00:17:56.861 --> 00:17:58.195
I could see that

00:17:58.229 --> 00:18:01.465
the sketch really didn't
look that much like him.

00:18:01.499 --> 00:18:03.835
Then why did you kick him?

00:18:03.869 --> 00:18:07.472
The police did say that these
mistakes happen all the time.

00:18:07.506 --> 00:18:10.074
Joy, I am so sorry
about everything.

00:18:10.108 --> 00:18:12.843
You should be.
I knew this would happen.

00:18:13.714 --> 00:18:16.664
Listen, of all the things
that happened tonight,

00:18:16.931 --> 00:18:18.748
the one thing that I
can't get out of my mind

00:18:18.782 --> 00:18:20.616
is the look on your
face when you thought

00:18:20.650 --> 00:18:23.452
I had finally done this
great thing for you.

00:18:23.486 --> 00:18:25.936
And then all I did
was disappoint you.

00:18:27.323 --> 00:18:30.124
I wasn't a good friend, and I will
never forgive myself for that.

00:18:30.158 --> 00:18:35.295
Of course you will.
And I will too.

00:18:35.329 --> 00:18:37.363
I thought Steve was
the perfect guy

00:18:37.398 --> 00:18:40.733
because everything he said were
things you knew I would love.

00:18:40.767 --> 00:18:43.593
Things only a best
friend would know.

00:18:43.695 --> 00:18:46.738
You know me well.

00:18:47.688 --> 00:18:48.688
Still, I--

00:18:51.749 --> 00:18:53.749
I would like you to have this.

00:18:56.745 --> 00:18:59.215
You know me <i>very</i> well!

00:19:00.737 --> 00:19:03.685
At least Joy's date
didn't have a dead wife.

00:19:03.720 --> 00:19:04.720
Or boobs.

00:19:06.856 --> 00:19:09.090
My date had both.

00:19:09.950 --> 00:19:12.925
So, Elka, when are you
gonna make it official?

00:19:12.960 --> 00:19:15.828
Oh...That's over.

00:19:15.862 --> 00:19:17.596
We started having problems.

00:19:17.630 --> 00:19:19.731
- Oh...
- What happened?

00:19:19.765 --> 00:19:22.901
Well, we got along fine,

00:19:22.935 --> 00:19:27.605
but he wouldn't go downtown,
if you know what I mean.

00:19:31.578 --> 00:19:32.828
What?

00:19:32.977 --> 00:19:35.577
I mean, there are so
many good restaurants

00:19:35.612 --> 00:19:39.014
and shops down there.

00:19:39.048 --> 00:19:41.382
I can't give that up.

00:19:41.417 --> 00:19:44.251
Of course you do.

00:19:44.286 --> 00:19:46.687
What'd you think I
was talking about?

00:19:46.721 --> 00:19:49.389
Nothing. Nothing at all.

00:19:51.625 --> 00:19:54.393
- Hi.
- Max...

00:19:54.428 --> 00:19:57.462
Listen, Elka,
I don't want to lose you.

00:19:57.497 --> 00:19:59.297
So if you're still up for it,

00:19:59.331 --> 00:20:02.866
I'm willing to try
going downtown.

00:20:06.170 --> 00:20:08.605
- You are?
- Yes.

00:20:08.639 --> 00:20:11.189
I just hope I won't
get lost down there.

00:20:14.576 --> 00:20:16.210
Oh, you won't.

00:20:16.244 --> 00:20:20.213
I have no problem
telling you where to go.

00:20:20.247 --> 00:20:25.317
It's just that it's so
dark and scary there.

00:20:25.351 --> 00:20:27.651
- Happy Birthday.
- Happy Birthday!

00:20:27.851 --> 00:20:38.051
